{"id": "first_solar-2026-09-17-007", "date": "2026-09-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": ["first_solar"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "First Solar drops TOPCon patent complaint", "content": "<p>The thin-film manufacturer withdrew its Section 337 filing before the USITC following new Section 232 import restrictions, while federal court patent battles against domestic and foreign manufacturers move forward.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/first-solar-drops-topcon-patent-complaint/\">First Solar drops TOPCon patent complaint</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/first-solar-drops-topcon-patent-complaint/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-17-008", "date": "2026-09-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh launches $123 million rooftop solar fund", "content": "<p>Bangladesh has launched a $123 million fund to provide concessional financing for rooftop solar and other renewable energy projects. The government is also seeking international funding to install 4 GW of rooftop solar before next summer.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/bangladesh-launches-123-million-rooftop-solar-fund/\">Bangladesh launches $123 million rooftop solar fund</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/bangladesh-launches-123-million-rooftop-solar-fund/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-17-009", "date": "2026-09-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Spain launches capacity market as grid investment rises above €17 billion", "content": "<p>Spain is introducing a new mechanism to remunerate generation, battery storage and demand for providing firm capacity and flexibility, while increasing planned electricity grid investment through 2030 to more than €17 billion ($19.5 billion). </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/spain-launches-capacity-market-as-grid-investment-rises-above-e17-billion/\">Spain launches capacity market as grid investment rises above €17 billion</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/spain-launches-capacity-market-as-grid-investment-rises-above-e17-billion/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-17-010", "date": "2026-09-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Scientists build 17%-efficient semi-transparent perovskite solar cell based on sputter-resistant aluminum oxide layer", "content": "<p>Researchers replaced the conventional 20 nm SnOₓ buffer layer with just 3 nm of ALD-deposited AlOₓ, which protected inverted perovskite cells from ITO sputtering damage while maintaining efficient charge extraction.<br />\nThe resulting devices achieved efficiencies above 17% in semi-transparent cells and 26% in perovskite-silicon tandems, while reducing material use and fabrication time.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/scientists-build-17-efficient-semi-transpa", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/scientists-build-17-efficient-semi-transparent-perovskite-solar-cell-based-on-sputter-resistant-aluminum-oxide-layer/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-17-011", "date": "2026-09-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "China targets perovskite solar, advanced batteries in five-year plan", "content": "<p>China has identified perovskite solar and next-generation batteries as strategic priorities in its 2026-30 industrial roadmap. The plan also calls for tighter oversight of manufacturing capacity and price competition.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/china-targets-perovskite-solar-advanced-batteries-in-five-year-plan/\">China targets perovskite solar, advanced batteries in five-year plan</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Glob", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/china-targets-perovskite-solar-advanced-batteries-in-five-year-plan/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-09-17-012", "date": "2026-09-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 38, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "PV inverters provide reactive power to Milan’s grid at night", "content": "<p>Researchers in Milan used PV inverters to supply 500 kVAr of reactive power to the distribution grid for four hours overnight. The trial showed that existing solar equipment can support voltage regulation even when it is not generating electricity.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/pv-inverters-provide-reactive-power-to-milans-grid-at-night/\">PV inverters provide reactive power to Milan’s grid at night</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">p", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/09/17/pv-inverters-provide-reactive-power-to-milans-grid-at-night/", "type": "rss"}]}
